; The default build target, stated explicitly so it does not fall back
; to dune's implicit (alias_rec all). The implicit definition would
; pull in every file target in the tree — which includes the
; runtime/wasm corpus: its fixture rules produce .actual files and the
; runs_bin binary, so a bare `dune build` used to spend ~50s executing
; the corpus (and re-ran it on every compiler relink) without even
; diffing the output.
;
; The default build is therefore compilation only: the installable
; binaries (emo, emo-lsp) plus every module and test executable under
; src/, bin/, and test/. Running Emo code stays opt-in — `dune test`
; for the @runtest suites (including the wasm smoke slice), and the
; wasm_spec / wasm_runs aliases for the full runtime/wasm corpora.

(alias
 (name default)
 (deps
  (alias_rec install)
  (alias_rec src/all)
  (alias_rec bin/all)
  (alias_rec test/all)))
